---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = 'October 2026';
const link = 'text-(--forest-light) underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-(--forest)';
---

<Base title="Accessibility" description="CityServ's commitment to accessibility and how to report a barrier.">
  <div class="bg-(--cream) min-h-screen py-12 px-4">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="mb-10">
        <nav class="text-xs text-(--text-muted) mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-(--forest) transition-colors">Home</a>
          <span class="mx-1.5 opacity-40" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
          <span class="text-(--forest)">Accessibility</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-(--forest)">Accessibility Statement</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-(--text-muted)">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
          Everyone should be able to find a way to serve their city. We want CityServ to work for people who use screen readers, keyboards, magnification, captions, or any other assistive technology.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-(--border) bg-white p-8 shadow-[var(--shadow)] space-y-8">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">Our goal</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA across cityserv.org.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">What we do</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            <li>Run automated accessibility checks (axe-core) on public pages before releases.</li>
            <li>Support full keyboard navigation, including a "Skip to main content" link.</li>
            <li>Label form fields and give errors in text, not color alone.</li>
            <li>Hide decorative illustrations from screen readers and stop animations when your device asks for reduced motion.</li>
            <li>Keep text contrast at or above WCAG AA ratios.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">Known limitations</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            <li>Organizations' own sign-up pages are run by those organizations, and we can't guarantee their accessibility. Tell us if one blocks you and we'll pass it on.</li>
            <li>The CAPTCHA on our forms is provided by Cloudflare Turnstile, which is designed to work without visual puzzles. If it stops you, email us and we'll handle your request directly.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">Report a barrier</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            If something on CityServ doesn't work for you, email <a href="mailto:contact@cityserv.org" class={link}>contact@cityserv.org</a> or use the <a href="/contact" class={link}>contact form</a>. Tell us the page and what happened. We aim to reply within 5 business days.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
